{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795083642,"nonce":"EkjU/Ji2cXG9fh48mAlROkHl8ek=","title":"jno.units.infer returns None for any expression built from a bound view","message":"An expression built from a bound field (`u = net(x, t).unit(\"K\").scalar.bind(x=x, t=t)`, then `u.t - alpha * u.xx`) is a `ScalarView` at the root. `jno.units.check` walks the graph under it and finds every mismatch, but the view itself is treated as an undeclared leaf, so `check(...).entries[-1]` and `jno.units.infer(...)` return `None` for the root. The node directly under the view has the right unit (K/s here). The unit tests build expressions from bare placeholders and never hit this; `rescale` already unwraps views (`_unwrap_view`), `check`/`infer` do not. Reproduction: the heat residual above with `alpha` a `jno.np.constant` with unit m^2/s; `jno.units.infer(u.t)` is also `None`. Fix: unwrap the view in `check` (and so `infer`), and test on a bound expression.","files":null}]}